# The Squiddy commit this graph is built against (AD-030-R17).
#
# WHY A FILE AND NOT A pyproject DEPENDENCY. Squiddy is a BUILD-TIME dependency of this graph, not
# a runtime dependency of the `seldon` package: `seldon/core/governed.py` reads a JSONL ledger and
# imports no Squiddy module, so a `pyproject.toml` entry would be a dependency Seldon never uses
# and would make Seldon un-installable wherever Squiddy is absent — which is every environment
# Seldon's own suite runs in. AD-030-R17 supersedes the `pyproject.toml` clause of AD-030-R10; the
# acyclicity and no-awareness clauses of R10 stand.
#
# WHY A COMMIT AND NOT A VERSION. The kit is one day old and its version number moves slower than
# its behaviour. The extraction this graph produces is a function of the parser, the assess
# criterion and the acquire adapter as they stood at a specific commit; a version range would make
# the corpus unreproducible without saying so.
#
# `make -C governed check-squiddy` verifies this, and every build target depends on it. To move the
# pin: check out the new commit, re-run `make -C governed kit-schema schema`, re-run the sweep, and
# update both values here in the same commit as the re-ingested ledger.

SQUIDDY_COMMIT=f23023750787ec3ca97c0a1f3b8d872445676b94
SQUIDDY_VERSION=0.2.0
